          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The term
            %em simplicial model category
            is short for
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} sSet
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mrow
                          %mi Quillen
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}_{Quillen}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+model+category"} enriched model category
          %p
            A simplicial model category is a model or presentation for an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            that is half way in between a bare
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            and a
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
          %p
            Specifically, a simplicial model category is an
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            together with the structure of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            on its underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
            such that both structures are compatible in a reasonable way.
          %p
            One important use of simplicial model categories comes from the fact that the full
            = succeed "-subcategory" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo ∘
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\circ \hookrightarrow C
            on the fibrant-cofibrant objects – which is not just
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            = succeed "-enhancement" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
          %p
            For generalizations of this construction with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            replaced by another
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
            see
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+homotopical+category"} enriched homotopical category
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The term
              %em simplicial model category
              for the notion described here is entirely standard, but in itself a bit suboptimal. More properly one would speak of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicially+enriched+category"} simplicially enriched category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial object
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
              (that for which the simplicial set of objects is discrete).
            %p
              The other caveat is that there are different model category structures on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              and hence even the term
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+model+category"} enriched model category
              is ambiguous.
            %p
              For instance the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+quasi-categories"} model structure for quasi-categories
              is an
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+model+category"} enriched model category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi sSet
                      %mi Joyal
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Joyal}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
              it is enriched over itself, hence is a
              = succeed "-enriched" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi sSet
                        %mi Joyal
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Joyal}
              = succeed "-enriched" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi sSet
                        %mi Quillen
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Quillen}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi sSet
                      %mi Joyal
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Joyal}
              is
              %em not
              a “simplicial model category”.
          %h2#definition Definition
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong simplicial model category
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+model+category"} enriched model category
              which is enriched over
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi sSet
                        %mi Quillen
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Quillen}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              equipped with its standard
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
          %p Spelled out, this means that a simplicial model category is
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                an
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
              %ul
                %li
                  which is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power"} powered
                  and
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensoring"} tensored
                  over
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            %li
              %p
                with the structure of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
                on the underlying category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
            %li
              %p
                such that for every cofibration
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i : A \to B
                and every fibration
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : X \to Y
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+powering"} pullback powering
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo ,
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi i
                            %mo *
                          %mo ×
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mo *
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mrow
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi A
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(B,X) \stackrel{i^* \times p_*}{\to} C(A,X) \times_{C(A,Y)} C(B,Y)
                is a
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} Kan fibration
              %ul
                %li
                  and such that this fibration is an acyclic fibration whenever either
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                  or
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                  are acyclic.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#EnrichmentTensoringCotensoring Enrichment, tensoring, and cotensoring
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            be a category equipped with the structure of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            and with that of an
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensoring"} tensored
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cotensoring"} cotensored
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
          #EquivalenceOfConditions.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The following conditions – that each make
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              into a
              %em simplicial model category
              – are equivalent:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensoring"} tensoring
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mo :
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo ×
                        %mi sSet
                        %mo →
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes : \mathcal{C} \times sSet \to \mathcal{C}
                  is a left
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+bifunctor"} Quillen bifunctor
              %li
                %p
                  %a{:href => "enriched+model+category#PullbackPowerAxiom"}> pullback-power axiom
                  \:
                %p
                  for any cofibration
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
                  and fibration
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo →
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
                  in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %msub
                          %mo ×
                          %mrow
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo ,
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\mathcal{C}(Y, A) \to \mathcal{C}(X, A) \times_{\mathcal{C}(X,B)} \mathcal{C}(Y,B)
                %p is a fibration, and is in addition a weak equivalence if either of the two morphisms is;
              %li
                %p
                  for any cofibration
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi sSet
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
                  and fibration
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo →
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
                  in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi A
                          %mi Y
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi A
                          %mi X
                        %msub
                          %mo ×
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi B
                              %mi X
                        %msup
                          %mi B
                          %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        A^Y \to A^X \times_{B^X} B^Y
                %p is a fibration, and is in addition a weak equivalence if either of the two morphisms is.
          %p
            This follows directly, by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joyal-Tierney+calculus"} Joyal-Tierney calculus
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensoring"} tensoring
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cotensoring"} cotensoring
            (as in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "enriched+model+category#MonoidalModelCategoryIsEnrichedModelOverItself"} this Prop.
          %p We list in the following some implications of these equivalent conditions.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            now be a simplicial model category.
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \mathcal{C}
              is fibrant, and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \hookrightarrow Y
              is a cofibration in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A^{Y} \to A^{X}
            %p
              is a fibration in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Apply prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EquivalenceOfConditions"}
              to the case of the cofibration
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
              and the fibration
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to *
              = succeed "\u201D" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mo *
                          %mi X
                    %msup
                      %mo *
                      %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A^Y \to A^X \times_{{*}^X} {*}^Y
            %p
              is a fibration. But
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo *
                      %mi Y
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mo *
                      %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {*}^Y = {*}^X =  {*}
              and hence the claim follows.
          %p Similarly we have
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary_2 Corollary
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathcal{C}
              is cofibrant and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \mathcal{C}
              is fibrant, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}(X,A)
              is fibrant in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Apply prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EquivalenceOfConditions"}
              to the cofibration
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ∅
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset \to X
              = succeed "\u201D" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ∅
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to *
              to find that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ∅
                        %mo ,
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{C}(X, A) \to \mathcal{C}(\emptyset, A) \times_{\mathcal{C}(\emptyset,*)} \mathcal{C}(X,*)
            %p
              is a fibration. But since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ∅
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset
              is initial and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *
              is terminal, all three simplicial sets in the fiber product on the right are the point, hence this is a fibration
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{C}(X,A) \to *
                    \\,.
          %h3#derived_homspaces Derived hom-spaces
          #DerivedHomSpaceBySimplicialFunctionComplex.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              any two objects and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P A
              a cofibrant and fibrant replacement, respectively,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Q
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi P
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}(Q X, P A)
              is the correct
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+hom-space"} derived hom-space
              between
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              (see the discussion there). In particular the full
              = succeed "-enriched" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
              on cofibrant fibrant objects is therefore an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicially+enriched+category"} sSet-enriched category
              which is fibrant in the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicially+enriched+categories"} model structure on simplicially enriched categories
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+coherent+nerve"} homotopy coherent nerve
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasi-category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              that is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presented
              by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            Although
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}(X,A)
            need not have the correct homotopy type for the mapping space if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is not cofibrant or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is not fibrant, simplicial notions of homotopy are still
            %em sufficient
            to detect the model-categorical ones.
          #SimplicialHomotopyImpliesHomotopy.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g:X\to A
              are simplicially homotopic (i.e. in the same connected component of the simplicial set
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}(X,A)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+homotopy+equivalence"} simplicial homotopy equivalence
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is a weak equivalence.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              This is Lemma 9.5.15 and Proposition 9.5.16 of
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Hirschhorn"} Hirschhorn
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#general General
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi sSet
                        %mi Quillen
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Quillen}
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
                and is hence naturally enriched, as a model category, over itself. This is the archetypical simplicial model category.
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
                for
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
                (
                %a{:href => "classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces#ModelStructureOnCompactlyGeneratedTopologicalSpaces"}> here
                ) is similarly enriched over itself. Under
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
                this also makes it a simplicial model category.
              %p
                (See also for instance
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "#GoerssSchemmerhorn06"} Goerss-Schemmerhorn 06, p. 26
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                any small
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+combinatorial+model+category"} simplicial combinatorial model category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+model+structure+on+functors"} global model structure on functors
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi proj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op}, A]_{proj}
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi inj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op},A]_{inj}
                are themselved simplicial combinatorial model categories. See
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} left Bousfield localization
                of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+simplicial+model+category"} combinatorial simplicial model category
                at any set of morphisms is again a combinatorial simplicial model category. Large classes of examples arise this way.
          %h3#SimpEquivMods Simplicial Quillen equivalent models
          %p
            While many model categories do not admit an
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi sSet
                        %mi Qu
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Qu}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+model+category"} enrichment
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            to a model category that does carry an
            = succeed "-enrichment." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi sSet
                      %mi Qu
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Qu}
          %p
            These are constructed as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} Bousfield localization
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+model+structures"} Reedy model structures
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+simplicial+objects"} category of simplicial objects
            in the given model category.
          #LocalizationOfStructureOnSimplicalObjects.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
