          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Dugger"} Dugger, theorem 5.2, theorem 5.7, theorem 6.1
          %p
            So in particular every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+proper+model+category"} left proper
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model category
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalent
            to a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              We first show that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+objects"} fibrant objects
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mi proj
                        %mo ,
                        %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]_{proj,S}
              are the objectwise fibrant objects all whose structure maps are weak equivalences in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mi Reedy
                        %mo ,
                        %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]_{Reedy,S}
              is directly analogous.
            %p
              By general properties of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} left Bousfield localization
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mi proj
                        %mo ,
                        %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]_{proj,S}
              are the projective fibrant objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              for which all induced morphisms on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+hom+spaces"} derived hom spaces
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                        %mo ,
                        %mi C
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mi proj
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi l
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}Hom_{[\Delta^{op}, C]_{proj}}(s \cdot(\Delta[k] \to \Delta[l]), X)
            %p
              are weak equivalences. Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              is cofibrant in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              by definition, also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \cdot \Delta[k]
              is cofibrant in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi C
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi proj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]_{proj}
            %p
              So for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in [\Delta^{op}, C]_{proj}
              fibrant, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet \in [\Delta^{op}, [\Delta^{op}, C]]
              be a
              %a{:href => "derived+hom+space#Framings"} simplicial framing
              for it. Notice that this means that for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet([n])
              is a simplicial framing for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X([n])
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi const
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} const X \to X_\bullet
                  being a weak equivalence means that for all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  the morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to X_n
                  is a weak equivalence, which means that for all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                  the morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X([k]) \to X_n([k])
                  is a weak equivalence.
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet
                  being fibrant in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                        %mo ,
                        %mi C
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mi proj
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mi Reedy
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, [\Delta^{op}, C]_{proj}]_{Reedy}
                  means that for all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\in \mathbb{N}
                  the morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mo ∂
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{\Delta[n]} \to X_{\partial \Delta[n]}
                  is a fibration in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi op
                          %mo ,
                          %mi C
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mi proj
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]_{proj}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \mathbb{N}
                  the morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mo ∂
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{\Delta[n]}([k]) \to X_{\partial \Delta[n]}([k])
                  is a fibration in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X([k])
                  is Reedy fibrant.
            %p Then we find
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℝ
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %msup
                                  %mi Δ
                                  %mi op
                                %mo ,
                                %mi C
                                %msub
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                                  %mi proj
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi s
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo →
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi l
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %msup
                                  %mi Δ
                                  %mi op
                                %mo ,
                                %mi C
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi s
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo →
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi l
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi s
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi l
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo →
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi ℝ
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi s
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi l
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo →
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\mathbb{R}Hom_{[\Delta^{op}, C]_{proj}}( s \cdot(\Delta[k] \to \Delta[l]), X)
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    Hom_{[\Delta^{op}, C]}(s \cdot(\Delta[k] \to \Delta[l]), X_\bullet)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    Hom_{C}(s , X_\bullet([l]) \to X_\bullet([k]))
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    \\mathbb{R}Hom_C(s, X([l]) \to X([k]))
                    \\,.
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              By assumption on the set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %p
              %br/
            %p
              Now we show that the weak equivalences in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mi proj
                        %mo ,
                        %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]_{proj,S}
              are precisely those morphisms that become weak equivalences under the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+colimit"} homotopy colimit
            %p
              By functorial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+resolution"} cofibrant resolution
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-out-of-three"} two-out-of-three
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+objects"} cofibrant objects
            %p
              By lemma
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HocolimOverHomotopyConstantSimplicialDiagram"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                        %mo ,
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi ℝ
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                        %mo ,
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi const
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi ℝ
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}Hom_{[\Delta^{op}, C]}(A,X)
                    \\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                    \\mathbb{R}Hom_{[\Delta^{op}, C]}(A, const Z)
                    \\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                    \\mathbb{R}Hom_{C}(\lim_\to A , Z)
            %p
              seen by computing the derived homs by
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "derived+hom+space#Framings"} simplicial framings
            %p
              Now, by properties of left
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} Bousfield localization
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
              is a weak equivalence if for all
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+objects"} local objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              the morphism of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+hom-spaces"} derived hom-spaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}Hom(A \to B, X)
              is a weak equivalence. Looking at the diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℝ
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %msup
                                  %mi Δ
                                  %mi op
                                %mo ,
                                %mi C
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℝ
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %msup
                                  %mi Δ
                                  %mi op
                                %mo ,
                                %mi C
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi const
                            %mi Z
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℝ
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %mo →
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Z
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℝ
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %msup
                                  %mi Δ
                                  %mi op
                                %mo ,
                                %mi C
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi B
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℝ
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %msup
                                  %mi Δ
                                  %mi op
                                %mo ,
                                %mi C
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi B
                            %mo ,
                            %mi const
                            %mi Z
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℝ
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %mo →
                            %mi B
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Z
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbb{R}Hom_{[\Delta^{op}, C]}(A,X)
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}&amp;
                    \\mathbb{R}Hom_{[\Delta^{op}, C]}(A, const Z)
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}&amp;
                    \\mathbb{R}Hom_{C}(\lim_\to A , Z)
                    \\\
                    \\uparrow &amp;&amp; \uparrow &amp;&amp; \uparrow
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{R}Hom_{[\Delta^{op}, C]}(B,X)
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}&amp;
                    \\mathbb{R}Hom_{[\Delta^{op}, C]}(B, const Z)
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}&amp;
                    \\mathbb{R}Hom_{C}(\lim_\to B , Z)
                    }
            %p
              we see that this is the case precisely if the vertical morphism on the right is a weak equivalence for all fibrant
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Z
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z \in C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lim_\to A \to \lim_\to B
              is a weak equivalence. Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              here are cofibrant in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi C
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi proj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]_{proj}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+colimits"} homotopy colimits
              (as discussed there).
            %p
              %br/
            %p
              Now we discuss that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi const
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mi proj
                        %mo ,
                        %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\lim_\to \dashv const) \colon C \to [\Delta^{op}, C]_{proj,S}
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi const
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} const \colon C \to [\Delta^{op}, C]_{proj}
              is clearly a right Quillen functor, hence we have a Quillen adjunction on the unlocalized structure. Moreover, by definition and by the above discussion, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi lim
                        %mo →
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lim_\to
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+colimit"} homotopy colimit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              to weak equivalences in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction#BehaviourUnderLocalization"} Quillen equivalence - Behaviour under localization
              are met, and hence it follows that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi const
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\lim_\to \dashv const)
              descends as a Quillen adjunction also to the localization.
            %p
              To see that this is a Quillen equivalence, it is sufficient to show that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in [\Delta^{op}, C]_{proj}
              cofibrant and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z \in C
              fibrant, a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lim_\to A \to Z
              is a weak equivalence in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              precisely if the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi const
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to const Z
              becomes a weak equivalence under the homotopy colimit.
            %p
              For this notice that we have a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi hocolim
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi hocolim
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi const
                            %mi Z
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi colim
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi colim
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi const
                            %mi Z
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    hocolim A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; hocolim(const Z)
                    \\\
                    \\big\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\big\downarrow
                    \\\
                    colim A &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; colim (const Z) &amp; \simeq Z
                    }
            %p
              and so our statement follows (by
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-out-of-3"} 2-out-of-3
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is cofibrant, by assumption, as before. To see that the right one is, too, consider the factorization
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi const
                    %mi Z
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi hocolim
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi const
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Z \to (const Z)_i \to hocolim (const Z) \to Z
            %p
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphism"} identity morphism
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in \mathbb{N}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HocolimOverHomotopyConstantSimplicialDiagram"}
              the first morphism is a weak equivalence, and hence so is the morphism in question.
            %p
              %br/
            %p
              Now we show that the weak equivalences in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mi Reedy
                        %mo ,
                        %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]_{Reedy,S}
              are the hocolim-equivalences.
            %p
              By a general result on
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories#FunctorialityOfLocalization"} functoriality of localization
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi id
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi id
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mi Reedy
                        %mo ,
                        %mi S
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ←
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mi proj
                        %mo ,
                        %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (id \dashv id ) : [\Delta^{op}, C]_{Reedy,S} \stackrel{\leftarrow}{\to} [\Delta^{op}, C]_{proj,S}
              is at least a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
            %p
              Let then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
              be a morphism in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]
              and consider two fibrant replacements
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi A
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi A
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi B
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi B
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\to&amp; \bar A &amp;\to &amp; \hat A
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    B &amp;\to&amp; \bar B &amp;\to&amp; \hat B
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the first one (
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar A \to \bar B
              ) is taken in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mi proj
                        %mo ,
                        %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]_{proj,S}
              and the second (
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat A \to \hat B
              ) in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi C
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi Reedy
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]_{Reedy}
            %p
              Assume first that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
              is a hocolim-equivalence. Then so is
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo →
                      %mover
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat A \to \hat B
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat A
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat B
              are fibrant in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi C
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi Reedy
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]_{Reedy}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]_{proj}
              by construction and at the same time all their structure maps are weak equivalences (use 2-out-of-3), so that they are in fact fibrant in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi C
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mrow
                          %mi proj
                          %mo ,
                          %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]_{proj,S}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat A \to \hat B
              is indeed even an objectwise weak equivalence. It follows then that so is
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mo →
                      %mover
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar A \to \bar B
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi C
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mrow
                          %mi Reedy
                          %mo ,
                          %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]_{Reedy, S}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi C
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mrow
                          %mi Reedy
                          %mo ,
                          %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]_{Reedy,S}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mi Reedy
                        %mo ,
                        %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]_{Reedy,S}
              it follows that also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
              is a weak equivalence there.
            %p
              By an analogous diagram chase, one shows the converse implication holds, that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
              being a weak equivalence in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mi Reedy
                        %mo ,
                        %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]_{Reedy,S}
              implies that it is a hocolim-equivalence.
            %p With this now it is clear that the identity adjunction above is in fact a Quillen equivalence.
            %p
              %br/
            %p
              Finally we show that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi const
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mi ev
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mi Reedy
                        %mo ,
                        %mi S
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi ev
                            %mn 0
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi const
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (const \dashv ev_0) : [\Delta^{op}, C]_{Reedy,S}
                    \\stackrel{\overset{const}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{ev_0}{\to}} C
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            %p
              First, it is immediate to check that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi const
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi Reedy
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} const \colon C \to [\Delta^{op}, C]_{Reedy}
              is left Quillen, and since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi id
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi Reedy
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mi Reedy
                        %mo ,
                        %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id : [\Delta^{op}, C]_{Reedy} \to [\Delta^{op}, C]_{Reedy,S}
              is left Quillen by definition of Bousfield localization, the above is at least a Quillen adjunction.
            %p
              To see that it is a Quillen equivalence, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in C
              be cofibrant and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mi Reedy
                        %mo ,
                        %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in [\Delta^{op}, C]_{Reedy,S}
              be fibrant – which by the above means that it is a simplicial resolution – and consider a morphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi const
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} const A \to X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to X_0
              is a weak equivalence in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %p
              To that end, find a cofibrant resolution
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi const
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} const \tilde A \to \tilde X
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi const
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} const A \to X
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]_{proj}
              and consider the diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ←
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi A
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mi colim
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi const
                            %mover
                              %mi A
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ←
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mover
                                %mi X
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                              %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mi colim
                            %mover
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\leftarrow}&amp;  \tilde A &amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}&amp;
                    colim(const \tilde A)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    X_0 &amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\leftarrow}&amp; \tilde X_0
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}&amp; colim \tilde X
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p The colimits on the right compute the homotopy colimit. By 2-out-of-3 it follows that the right vertical morphism is a weak equivalence precisely if the left vertical morphisms is.
            %p
              %br/
            %p
              Finally it remains to show that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mi Reedy
                        %mo ,
                        %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]_{Reedy,S}
              is a simplicially enriched model category. (…)
          #AUniquenessTheorem.num_theorem
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              %strong (uniqueness)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mi C
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s C \coloneqq [\Delta^{op}, C]
              such that
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  every morphism that is degreewise a weak equivalence in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  is a weak equivalence in
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi s
                          %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s C
              %li
                %p
                  the cofibrations are those of the
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+model+structure"} Reedy model structure
              %li
                %p
                  the fibrant objects are the Reedy-fibrant objects whose face and degeneracy maps are weak equivalences in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#RezkSchwedeShipley"} Rezk, Schwede &amp; Shipley, theorem 3.1
          .proof
            %h6#proof_5 Proof
            %p
              By theorem
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalizationOfReedyOnSimplicialObjects"}
              at least one such model structure exists. By the discussion at
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "model+category#RedundancyInTheAxioms"} model category – Redundancy of the axioms
          #DerivedHomBySimplicialReplacement.num_cor
            %h6#corollary_3 Corollary
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+model+category"} left proper
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+hom-space"} derived hom-space
              between two objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, A
              may be computed by
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  choosing a cofibrant replacement
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  in
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %li
                %p
                  choosing a Reedy fibrant replacement
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat A
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi const
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} const A
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                        %mo ,
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]
                  such that all face and degeneracy maps are weak equivalences,
            %p setting
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Maps
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Maps(X,A)
                    \\;\colon\;
                    [n] \mapsto Hom_C(\hat X, \hat A_n)
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_6 Proof
            %p
              By theorem
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalizationOfReedyOnSimplicialObjects"}
              we may compute the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+hom+space"} derived hom space
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mi Reedy
                        %mo ,
                        %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]_{Reedy,S}
              after the inclusion
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi const
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} const \colon C \to [\Delta^{op}, C]
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mi Reedy
                        %mo ,
                        %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]_{Reedy,S}
              is a simplicial model category, by prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DerivedHomSpaceBySimplicialFunctionComplex"}
              the derived hom space is given by the simplicial function complex between a cofibrant replacement of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi const
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} const X
              and a fibrant replacement of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi const
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} const A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X
              is cofibrant, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi const
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} const \hat X
              is already Reedy cofibrant, and by the theorem
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat A
              as stated is a a fibrant resolution of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi const
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} const A
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi op
                            %mo ,
                            %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi const
                            %mover
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %mo ,
                            %mover
                              %mi A
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %msup
                                  %mi Δ
                                  %mi op
                                %mo ,
                                %mi C
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi const
                            %mover
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo ,
                            %mover
                              %mi A
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %msup
                                  %mi Δ
                                  %mi op
                                %mo ,
                                %mi C
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi const
                            %mover
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %msup
                              %mover
                                %mi A
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                              %mrow
                                %mi Δ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %mi n
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mover
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mover
                                %mi A
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    [\Delta^{op}, C](const \hat X, \hat A)_n
                    \&amp; =
                    Hom_{[\Delta^{op}, C]}((const \hat X) \cdot \Delta[n], \hat A)
                    \\\
                    \&amp;  \simeq
                    Hom_{[\Delta^{op}, C]}((const \hat X) , \hat A^{\Delta[n]})
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    Hom_C(\hat X, \hat A_n)
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
          %p
            There is also a version for
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+model+categories"} stable model categories
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+model+category"} proper
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+model+category"} stable model category
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalent
              to a simplicial model category
          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#RezkSchwedeShipley"} Rezk, Schwede &amp; Shipley, prop 1.3
          %h3#combinatorial_simplicial_model_categories Combinatorial simplicial model categories
          %p
            A particularly important type of simplicial model categories are those that are also
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model categories
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+simplicial+model+category"} combinatorial simplicial model category
            is precisely a
            %em presentation
            for a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} locally presentable (∞,1)-category
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dugger%27s+theorem"} Dugger's theorem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%28CombModCat%29"} Ho(CombModCat)
            %li
              %p
                %span.newWikiWord
                  simplicial monoidel model category
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/simplicial+monoidel+model+category"} ?
          %h2#references References
          %p The definition originates in
          %ul
            %li#Quillen67
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Quillen"}> Daniel Quillen
              , chapter II, section 2 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Homotopical+Algebra"} Homotopical Algebra
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 43
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/BFb0097438"} doi:10.1007/BFb0097438
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li#Hirschhorn
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Philip+Hirschhorn"}> Philip Hirschhorn
                , Chapter 9 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Model Categories and Their Localizations
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/surv-99-s/"} ISBN:978-0-8218-4917-0
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.gbv.de/dms/goettingen/360115845.pdf"} pdf toc
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~aar/papers/hirschhornloc.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
                , section A.3 in
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
                (2009)
            %li
              %p
                %span.newWikiWord>
                  Garth Waner
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Garth+Waner"} ?
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Categorical Homotopy Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://hdl.handle.net/1773/19589"} hdl:1773/19589
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://digital.lib.washington.edu/researchworks/bitstreams/0082c74f-f4e0-4578-a44e-d57a0ea29112/download"} pdf
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Waner-CategoricalHomotopy.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emily+Riehl"}> Emily Riehl
                , §3.8 and §11.4 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categorical+Homotopy+Theory"} Categorical Homotopy Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781107261457"} doi:10.1017/CBO9781107261457
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.jhu.edu/~eriehl/cathtpy.pdf"} pdf
          %p Further review:
          %ul
            %li#GoerssSchemmerhorn06
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Goerss"}> Paul Goerss
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kirsten+Schemmerhorn"} Kirsten Schemmerhorn
              = succeed "," do
                %em Model categories and simplicial methods
              = succeed "," do
                %em Interactions between Homotopy Theory and Algebra
              %strong 436
              AMS (2007) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.AT/0609537"}> arXiv:math.AT/0609537
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1090/conm/436"} doi:10.1090/conm/436
          %p On Quillen-equivalent simplicial enhancements of model categories:
          %ul
            %li#RezkSchwedeShipley
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Rezk"}> Charles Rezk
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"} Stefan Schwede
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brooke+Shipley"} Brooke Shipley
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Simplicial structures on model categories and functors
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0101162"} arXiv:0101162
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/pdfplus/25099071.pdf"} jstor
            %li#Dugger
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Dugger"}> Dan Dugger
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Replacing model categories with simplicial ones
                %strong 353
                12 (2001) 5003-5027 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.ams.org/journals/tran/2001-353-12/S0002-9947-01-02661-7"}> ams:S0002-9947-01-02661-7
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.ams.org/journals/tran/2001-353-12/S0002-9947-01-02661-7/S0002-9947-01-02661-7.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Dugger01
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Dugger"}> Daniel Dugger
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Combinatorial+model+categories+have+presentations"} Combinatorial model categories have presentations
                %strong 164
                (2001) 1 177-201 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0007068"}> arXiv:math/0007068
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1006/aima.2001.2015"} doi:10.1006/aima.2001.2015
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (cf.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dugger%27s+theorem"} Dugger's theorem
